Each parameter set becomes its own test with its own name, result and traceback. A loop stops at the first failing value, hides which input failed and reports one result for everything.

```python
import pytest

@pytest.mark.parametrize("a,b,expected", [(1, 2, 3), (0, 0, 0), (-1, 1, 0)])
def test_add(a, b, expected):
    assert a + b == expected

